    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "zero-dimensional mononuclear coordination compounds → stability"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] design Zn(II)-uniconazole complexes with smaller HOMO-LUMO energy gaps → complexes 1-4 have HOMO-LUMO gaps of 0.0578, 0.0946, 0.1053, and 0.1245 eV versus 0.1247 eV for the free ligand, and the smaller gaps correlate with higher antifungal activity"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] change the Zn(II) counter anion to tune the complex structure → the SO4^2- containing complex forms a 1D polymer chain and shows better antifungal activity than the other anion-derived complexes"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "complex 1 vs complex 2: winner=subject_a on antifungal_activity_ranking"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "complex 1 vs complexes 2-4: winner=subject_a on antifungal_activity"
    },
    {
      "title": "Failure",
      "body": "[performance_regression] use simple metal-salt and uniconazole mixtures instead of forming discrete Zn(II)-uniconazole complexes: the simple mixtures do not enhance antifungal activity over the free ligand at the same mass concentration"
    }
